WEBVTT

00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:07.682
In this video, you will get the free SoCal Lights app for iPhone and iPad, and see the map, your hearts, and a route.

00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:08.951
We start on the website.

00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:12.929
On SoCal Lights dot app, open Tutorials.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:14.810
Tap Download on the App Store.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.635
The app is free for iPhone and iPad.

00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:23.230
Or open the App Store on your iPhone or iPad, and search for SoCal Lights.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.209
Tap Get.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:25.865
When it finishes, tap Open.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.086
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:31.727 --> 00:00:34.277
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:36.895
Then tap Allow.

00:00:40.154 --> 00:00:41.394
This is the app.

00:00:41.394 --> 00:00:47.303
It opens on the same map as the website, with the same places, seasons, and filters.

00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:50.924
Every update to the website reaches the app by itself.

00:00:50.924 --> 00:00:53.497
When you see a place you want to visit, tap the heart.

00:00:55.774 --> 00:00:57.437
That saves it to your favorites.

00:00:57.437 --> 00:00:58.501
I will save two.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.829
Now tap Favorites.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.399
Your hearts are here, put in a sensible driving order.

00:01:04.399 --> 00:01:08.507
Route these opens in Google Maps, Apple Maps, or Waze.

00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:11.174
Tap the maps app name, and pick the one you use.

00:01:12.736 --> 00:01:14.972
When you are ready to go, tap Route these.

00:01:16.656 --> 00:01:18.605
Your maps app takes the stops.

00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:21.971
A long list is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:21.971 --> 00:01:24.135
Waze takes one stop at a time.

00:01:24.135 --> 00:01:25.526
Tap the X to close.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:32.164
Everything you just saw also works on the web, at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:35.613
Next up: Find contests.
